sdata> -- Issue #69: a script error raised by an Immediate-tier command mid-session
sdata> -- must not crash Run_REPL or leave it stuck -- the buffer resets and the
sdata> -- REPL keeps accepting input afterward. TABLES on an unknown crossing
sdata> -- variable errors immediately; the subsequent PRINT/RUN/TABLES sequence
sdata> -- proves the REPL's own exception handler (not batch's Execute) recovered
sdata> -- cleanly and state (Pending_Deferred etc.) is still consistent.
sdata> USE "tests/data/freq_select.csv"
Dataset opened: tests/data/freq_select.csv
sdata> TABLES NOPE$
Error: TABLES: unknown variable 'NOPE$'
sdata> PRINT "still alive"
sdata> RUN
still alive
still alive
still alive
still alive
still alive
still alive
RUN complete. 6 records and 3 variables processed.
sdata> TABLES PRODUCT$
Frequency table for PRODUCT$

PRODUCT$ Frequency Percent Cum_Freq Cum_Percent
A 3 50.00 3 50.00
B 3 50.00 6 100.00
Total 6 100.00

TABLES complete.
sdata> QUIT
